# plans/BUILD_AND_DEPENDENCY_SYSTEM_REDESIGN.md §4.8: the nodes of ONE DAG level
# run `-j N` at a time. `alpha` and `beta` have no edge between them, so with
# `-j 2` both compile concurrently — and then their `Building …` lines and the
# C compiler's chatter INTERLEAVE, which is why only the summary line is
# compared. That line is what the case is about: every node ran and succeeded
# under concurrency.
# YO_ASYNC_STRICT=1 arms C37's nested-event-loop guard for the RUNNER itself:
# a level's nodes are spawned tasks now, so any blocking wait the scheduler uses
# to collect them (`join_all`, `race`, a plain awaiting helper) re-enters the
# event loop from inside a task and aborts here. That is how this slice's own
# first draft was caught
# (issues/fixed/build-scheduler-join-all-nests-the-event-loop.md) — by a
# different case, which is why the guard now rides the case that owns the
# feature.
env=YO_ASYNC_STRICT=1
timeout=900
stdout_keep_match=Build Summary: [0-9]+/[0-9]+ steps succeeded
